cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LocalGovBench, please cite this research software."
type: software
title: "LocalGovBench: Disclosure Affordances in Public AI and Algorithm Registers"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-07-23"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21500899"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research repository for studying schema disclosure affordance
  and planned record-level realization in public AI and algorithm registers,
  using Disclosure Functions v1. Includes a frozen specification layer,
  observed-field schema inventory tooling, and a human schema-coding system.
  Does not provide governance readiness or maturity scores, shortfall scores,
  compliance scores, composite indices, or jurisdiction rankings. Historical
  LocalGovBench v0.1.0 (Governance Readiness Benchmark) remains available as a
  provenance archive (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20543779) and is not the active
  analytical framework.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - public sector
  - algorithm registers
  - AI inventories
  - algorithmic transparency
  - disclosure affordance
  - schema coding
  - reproducibility
  - European Union
